- Why? About the book?

990
01:51:03,418 --> 01:51:05,090
- No, it's Frank.
- Donnie...

991
01:51:05,178 --> 01:51:07,373
Time is running out! We gotta go.

992
01:51:53,658 --> 01:51:56,809
Donnie, nobody's here.
Let's just forget about it.

993
01:51:58,698 --> 01:52:00,609
"Cellar door."

994
01:52:00,698 --> 01:52:01,972
What?

995
01:53:04,538 --> 01:53:06,176
Donnie! Donnie!

996
01:53:10,138 --> 01:53:11,332
Donnie!

997
01:53:12,378 --> 01:53:15,734
- Why the fuck are you here?
- Oh, my God!

998
01:53:19,898 --> 01:53:21,729
- You're dead!
- What do we do?

999
01:53:21,818 --> 01:53:23,888
- Shit!
- Leave them alone!

1000
01:53:27,978 --> 01:53:30,572
Don't fucking move!
Don't fucking move!

1001
01:53:39,338 --> 01:53:40,851
There's a car!

1002
01:53:42,538 --> 01:53:45,052
- Get the hell out of here!
- Come on!

1003
01:53:46,058 --> 01:53:48,367
Seth, a car's coming. Let's go!

1004
01:53:48,458 --> 01:53:50,892
I have a bigger knife now.

1005
01:53:52,138 --> 01:53:53,173
Fuck!

1006
01:54:00,538 --> 01:54:02,847
Did you call the fucking cops?

1007
01:54:02,938 --> 01:54:05,611
- Deus ex machina.
- What did you just say?

1008
01:54:07,698 --> 01:54:10,974
- What the fuck did you say?
- Our saviour.

1009
01:54:15,538 --> 01:54:16,368
Donnie!

1010
01:54:47,458 --> 01:54:48,777
Frank...

1011
01:55:14,498 --> 01:55:15,931
Is she dead?

1012
01:55:25,018 --> 01:55:28,567
What were you guys doing
in the middle of the road?!

1013
01:55:36,298 --> 01:55:37,413
Go home!

1014
01:55:38,698 --> 01:55:41,496
Go and tell your parents
everything will be ok.

1015
01:55:43,058 --> 01:55:44,377
Go!

1016
01:56:12,098 --> 01:56:17,616
The storm is coming.
You must hurry.

1017
01:58:51,258 --> 01:58:53,488
I'm going home.

1018
02:00:59,938 --> 02:01:03,977
Dear Roberta Sparrow,
I've reached the end of your book

1019
02:01:04,458 --> 02:01:07,530
and there's so many things
I need to ask you.

1020
02:01:08,378 --> 02:01:11,575
Sometimes I'm afraid
of what you might tell me.

1021
02:01:15,498 --> 02:01:17,534
Sometimes I'm afraid
that you'll tell me

1022
02:01:17,618 --> 02:01:20,007
this is not a work of fiction.

1023
02:01:20,778 --> 02:01:25,215
I can only hope that the answer
will come to me in my sleep.

1024
02:01:26,458 --> 02:01:29,131
I hope that when the world ends

1025
02:01:29,218 --> 02:01:32,290
I can breathe a sigh of relief

1026
02:01:32,378 --> 02:01:36,053
because there will be
so much to look forward to.

1027
02:06:22,138 --> 02:06:24,652
Hey. What's going on?

1028
02:06:26,538 --> 02:06:30,895
Horrible accident.
My neighbour... got killed.

1029
02:06:32,538 --> 02:06:36,053
- What happened?
- Got smushed by a jet engine.

1030
02:06:42,618 --> 02:06:44,290
What was his name?

1031
02:06:44,818 --> 02:06:47,048
Donnie. Donnie Darko.

1032
02:06:49,978 --> 02:06:52,333
I feel bad for his family.

1033
02:06:53,058 --> 02:06:54,491
Yeah.

1034
02:07:01,898 --> 02:07:03,854
Did you know him?

1035
02:07:07,058 --> 02:07:08,889
No.
